From 8aecabf25df3976f5e7fe5f67f40e619434b36f0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pwtail <abvit89s@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 02:24:49 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 08/10] Fix MatchError shadowing, compile leak, and .0 temp
 leak

- Desugar failures to raise __import__('builtins').MatchError(...) so a user
  variable named MatchError cannot shadow the real exception.
- Allocate parser temp structs (match_assign_binding/case, pipe_step/case)
  from the arena instead of leaking them via PyMem_Malloc; use a single shared
  interned .0 temp instead of a per-compile counter.
- Desugar irrefutable assert patterns (bare capture/wildcard, no guard) to a
  plain 'match e: case P: pass' without a walrus, so no .0 temp leaks into scope.
---
 Lib/test/test_eelang_v3.py             |  26 ++++-
 Parser/action_helpers.c                | 143 ++++++++++++++-----------
 Parser/pegen.c                         |   1 -
 Parser/pegen.h                         |   1 -
 Tools/build/generate_global_objects.py |   2 +-
 5 files changed, 108 insertions(+), 65 deletions(-)

